.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kirchhausen</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cdc42 is required for PIP2-induced actin polymerization and early development but not for cell viability</article-title><source>Curr. Biol.</source><volume>10</volume><year>2000</year><fpage>758</fpage><lpage>765</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10898977</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Egileetal1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Egile</surname><given-names>C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Loisel</surname><given-names>T.P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Laurent</surname><given-names>V.</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Pantaloni</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Sansonetti</surname><given-names>P.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Carlier</surname><given-names>F.-F.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Activation of the Cdc42 effector N-WASP by the <italic>Shigella flexneria</italic> IcsA protein promotes actin nucleation by Arp2/3complex and bacterial actin-based motility</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><volume>146</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>1319</fpage><lpage>1332</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10491394</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Finanetal1996"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Finan</surname><given-names>P.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Soames</surname><given-names>C.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilson</surname><given-names>L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Nelson</surname><given-names>D.L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>D.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Truon</surname><given-names>O.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hsuan</surname><given-names>J.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kellie</surname><given-names>S.</given-n